et cap on $285M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 9.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 12.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 631% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u20